From c4b54bade964c9858c2bad1897d639c34694a849 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:58:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 058/147] media: qcom: camss: Add SM8350 support

SM8350 has Titan 580. The vendor camera driver runs its CSID580 with
the CSID480 data and its VFE580 with the VFE480 tables (only the RDI1
input mux shift of the CAMIF lite and the CAMIF data differ, which the
RDI path here does not use), and the register map is that of SM8250
plus a third full IFE at 0xacef000 (CSID2 inside it at +0x1200, the
same layout). So the SM8250 ops serve:

- CSID/VFE: three full and two lite instances on csid_ops_gen2 and
  vfe_ops_480, the CSID inside the VFE region as on SM8250; the CSID
  base is now chosen by is_lite, not by index, because the third
  instance is a full one on SM8350.
- IFE clock rates of the SM8350 camera clock controller (338, 475,
  600, 720 MHz), CSID and CPHY RX at 400 MHz.
- CSIPHY: the SM8250 resources, with the D-PHY lane settings of the
  vendor csiphy v1.2.3 table (lane_regs_sm8350).

This needs the SM8350 camera clock controller and the qcom,sm8350-camss
binding, which follow in this series.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
